# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# JARVIS runtime data — personal, regenerable, or large.
# Memory databases hold private facts about you. Keep them local,
# back them up separately (encrypted), never push them to a remote.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
memory/
recordings/
transcripts/
screenshots/
renders/
jarvis/data/
snap.png
cache/
.cache/

# Audio / video artifacts
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.flac
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm

# …EXCEPT the media test fixtures. The rules above are meant to keep stray
# recordings out of the repo, but they also silently swallowed the GPS-tagged
# .mov that moment-media-iphone.spec.ts asserts against — the test would have
# been committed without the file it reads and failed only in CI. These two
# fixtures are small, deliberate, and synthetic (ffmpeg testsrc + exiftool
# tags); they contain no real location and no real footage.
!spotme/backend/test/fixtures/media/*.mov
!spotme/backend/test/fixtures/media/*.mp4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

